Nicholas "'''nitr0'''" Cannella {{born}} is an [[:Category:United States|American]] professional ''[[Counter-Strike 2]]'' player and a former ''[[Counter-Strike: Global Offensive]]'' and ''[[Counter-Strike]]'' player. He is among the most accomplished North American players, having won the [[Intel/Grand_Slam/2|second Intel Grand Slam]] with [[Team Liquid]] in 2019. 

nitr0 initially retired on August 14, 2020 to pursue a career in ''[[valorant:nitr0|VALORANT]]'' after being signed by ''[[valorant:100 Thieves|100 Thieves]]'', but came back to the game following [[Team Liquid]]'s restructuring in late 2021. <ref>{{cite web|url=https://twitter.com/100Thieves/status/1294348112505389056|title=Welcome @nitr0 to 100 Thieves VALORANT|author=[[valorant:100 Thieves|100 Thieves]]|date=2020-08-14}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=https://twitter.com/TeamLiquidCS/status/1482412270621761537|title=Welcome back, @nitr0|author=[[Team Liquid]]|date=2022-01-15}}</ref> He announced his second retirement as a player on May 27, 2023 before returning to ''[[valorant:nitr0|VALORANT]]'' with ''[[valorant:M80|M80]]'' on January 4, 2024. <ref>{{cite web|url=https://twitter.com/nitr0/status/1662226546416037888|title=My next chapter!|author='''nitr0'''|date=2023-05-27}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=https://twitter.com/M80gg/status/1742984250842910734|title=M80 VALORANT is back|author=[[M80]]|date=2024-01-04}}</ref> He returned to ''Counter-Strike'' once again on July 4, 2024 upon joining [[NRG]]. <ref>{{cite_web|url=https://x.com/NRGgg/status/1808923732615819715|title=Every team needs a captain|author=[[M80]]|date=2024-07-04}}</ref>

